# Narset, Parter of Veils (Bot2's) and Underrealm Lich (Bot1's): "if an opponent's first draw is replaced (by Underrealm Lich's
# ability, for example), that draw didn't happen and Narset won't stop the next draw (which may also be replaced by Underrealm
# Lich's ability)" (Narset's ruling; CR 121.2b, 614.6). Bot1's turn 3 draw for the turn is replaced by the Lich, so Bot1 has
# drawn no card this turn, and each of Ancestral Recall's three draws can still happen - and is replaced by the Lich too.
# Bot1 takes four cards into its hand this turn; had the first been drawn, Narset would have left it no more.

[Bot1 Deck]
Island
Black Lotus
Mox Emerald
Mox Sapphire
Underrealm Lich
Ancestral Recall
Plains
Island x20

[Bot2 Deck]
Black Lotus
Narset, Parter of Veils
Swamp x5
Swamp x20

[Actions]
